  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR is slice S3a of #2629. The issue is too large for one PR (see the escalation comment of 2026-11-22). The S2 kernel cut only from the empty floor. A playback could therefore not continue from a keyframe on the GPU. This slice adds the incremental start in `camcraft-gpu`:\n\n- `crates/gpu/src/cut.wgsl`: a new entry point `cs_encode`. It turns a layer (the f32 bits that `cs_decode` writes) back into order-preserving keys, in place.\n- `CutKernel::cut_into`: cuts a batch into a buffer of the caller (encode, cut, decode). It reads nothing back. S3c uses it on the `Scene.cut` buffer of the render device.\n- `CutKernel::run_onto`: the same cut on its own buffer, read back.\n- `cut_cpu_onto`: the CPU law of the same cut. With the max law it is bit-exact to the one-batch cut.\n- `cut_onto_or_cpu` and `cut_onto_or_cpu_on`: the run-time choice of `cut_or_cpu`. These conditions give the CPU law, with the reason, logged one time:\n  - `CAMCRAFT_GPU_COMPUTE=off`;\n  - no adapter, or no compute;\n  - a lost device, or a kernel error;\n  - a failed spot check (`spot_check_onto`).\n- A base layer with the wrong texel count or a non-finite value is refused by name.\n- `cut_gpu.rs` is split along the buffer seam into `cut_buf.rs` (the 400-line law). The code that moved is not changed, except that `first += ITEMS_PER_DISPATCH` is now a saturating add.\n\nDisplay only. The verdict (`simulate_document`) and the post gate do not change.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/gpu/tests/cut_onto.rs`)\n\n1. `the_gpu_cut_onto_a_keyframe_matches_the_cpu_law_or_skips_by_name`: GPU against CPU on a small fixture (ball, tilted flat, level flat), within `SPOT_MARGIN_FRACTION` of the claim margin. It also checks that `cut_into` equals `run_onto` bit for bit, and that a short target buffer is refused. When there is no adapter, the test prints a named SKIP. With `CAMCRAFT_REQUIRE_GPU=1` it fails. Reading on this machine: `\"Microsoft Basic Render Driver\" via Dx12`, max |GPU - CPU law| = 0.\n2. `the_off_switch_takes_the_cpu_law_by_name`: a child process with `CAMCRAFT_GPU_COMPUTE=off` gets `CutPath::Cpu` with a reason that names the switch, and the CPU bits.\n3. `a_lost_device_takes_the_cpu_law_and_never_crashes`: a child process destroys the shared device (the real device-lost callback). Then `run_onto` gives an `Err`, `cut_into` does not panic, and the two fallback entries give the CPU bits. The shared path names the loss.\n\nAlso: `the_incremental_cpu_law_is_the_one_batch_cut_bit_for_bit`, `a_bad_base_layer_is_refused_by_name`, and the unit test `a_layer_uploads_as_its_little_endian_bits`.\n\nNew top-level test file: `camcraft-gpu` has no directory suite. This binary must touch only the one shared `wgpu` instance of its process (#3589). It runs the switch and device-loss cases as child processes of itself. `cut_parity.rs` is at 378 lines.\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6): green. The steps were gpu lib, gpu:cut_onto and gpu:cut_parity.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-gpu --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-gpu`: all suites green.\n- `camcraft-ui` lib tests: 1587 passed, 0 failed, 8 ignored (`cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib`).\n- Heavy lanes: none (a P2 PR gets no heavy step).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A hardware adapter. The GPU parity ran on the WARP software adapter only. Precondition 1 of the S2 review (parity on a hardware adapter) is still open.\n- No viewport code changes in this slice, so there are no screenshots.\n\n## What remains of #2629\n\n- S3b: the worker protocol in `camcraft-app`. On the GPU path, the worker sends the twin work for each frame. It keeps CPU checkpoints for the fallback and for the operations that the twin refuses.\n- S3c: the UI side in `crates/ui/src/trace/`. It dispatches `cut_into` off the UI thread on the render device. It keeps the keyframe store in a VRAM budget, and it falls back to the CPU frames on any error.\n- The path choice by batch size and adapter kind, from hardware timings.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/2629-gpu-cut-onto.md`.\n\nEffort: max (the issue was escalated from effort:high before this run).\n\nChangelog: none (internal kernel entries; the viewport does not use them yet)\n\nRefs #2629\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
